With associated types in traits, you can define placeholder types within a trait, where the concrete type is determined by the implementing type. This approach provides flexibility for trait implementers to choose the specific types that make sense for their implementation. Associated types within a trait are declared using the following syntax:

```
type name_of_associated_type
```

Let’s add the associated type to the definition of the trait, as in the following example:

```
trait DistanceThreeHours {
    type Distance;
    fn distance_in_three_hours(&self) -> Self::Distance;
}
